    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62793" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεχαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			) <i>of</i> or <i>for a couch</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλλάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1182
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theognost.
				<u>Can.</u>
				9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4
				</span></i>
			) <i>in the nest</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνων
				ὑπερδέδοικε λεχαίων</span> for her <i>nestlings</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				292
			</span></i> (Lachm., for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεχέων</span>).</div>
